# Build context rules for packages/witness/deploy/Dockerfile (the context is the repository root).
# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile in place of a root .dockerignore.
#
# An allowlist: the image needs the workspace manifests, the lockfile and two packages. Everything
# else stays out of the context, including local histories, owner keys and witness data directories
# a developer may have lying around (*.owner-key.json, witness-key.json), .git and host node_modules.
*

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!tsconfig.base.json

# The packages the image is built from. The build installs with --filter, so pnpm checks only these
# two importers against the lockfile; the other workspace packages need not be in the context.
# (Exceptions are plain directory prefixes on purpose: wildcards in "!" rules are not honoured for
# files inside excluded directories by every builder.)
!packages/core
!packages/witness

# ...without build output, installed modules, tests or local state.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tgz
packages/*/test
packages/*/bench
packages/*/coverage
**/*.owner-key*.json
**/witness-key.json
**/.DS_Store
